They are derived from Set I of the disjunctively constrained knapsack problem, distributed by
Z. Wei and J.-K. Hao on Mendeley Data under CC BY 4.0 (doi:10.17632/gb5hhjkygd.1), whose instances were
introduced by M. Hifi and M. Michrafy (2006) and by Z. Quan and L. Wu (2017). Changes: each instance
keeps the number of items, the capacity, the profits, the weights and the conflict graph of its source,
writes the edges sorted, and adds quadratic profits as described in README.md. The reference values
are computed from the DCKP solution certificates of Wei, Hao, Ren and Glover (2023).
